==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/grat/|lang=ru}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|ru}} {{recons|gradъ|lang=sla-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{recons|greh₃d-|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with Lithuanian [[grúodas]] (Balto-Slavic *grōda-), Latin {{term|grando|grandō|lang=la}}, Old Armenian {{term|կարկուտ|sc=Armn|lang=xcl|tr=karkut}} (from Proto-Armenian *gagrōdo-), Old Indic *hrādúniṣ, and possibly with English {{term|grind}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun|g=m|a=i|tr=grad}}

# {{meteorology|lang=ru}} [[hail]]
#:* Град [[идти|идёт]] — ''It’s hailing.''
# {{meteorology|lang=ru}} [[shower]], [[rain]]
# [[volley]], [[shower]]
#:* град [[пуля|пуль]] — ''hail of bullets''

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-inan-1-unc||гра́д}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{etyl|cu|ru}} {{term|sc=Cyrs|градъ|tr=grádŭ|lang=cu}}, which is a reflex of Proto-Slavic {{recons|gordъ||settlement, enclosed place|lang=sla-pro}}, whence also Russian {{term|sc=Cyrl|город|tr=górod|lang=ru}} was normally inherited by [[w:pleophony|pleophony]]. Old Church Slavonic word shows [[w:liquid metathesis|liquid metathesis]] characteristic of South Slavic area.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun|tr=grad|g=m|a=i}}

# {{context|pоetic|antiquated}} [[town]], [[city]], used as a common city name suffix ([[Волгоград]], [[Калининград]], [[Ленинград]])
#:* [[стольный]] град — ''capital (city)'' (''modern Russian'': [[столица]])

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-inan-1||гра́д}}

=====Related terms=====
* [[город]]

===Etymology 3===
From {{etyl|la|ru}} {{term|gradus|lang=la}}.

====Abbreviation====
'''град.''' ([[градус]], ''grádus'')

# [[degree]]

